        {"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","@id":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/addyosmani_practical-loop-engineering-activity-7494279218160103424-6ys6","datePublished":"2026-08-15T06:30:02.541Z","headline":"\"Practical Loop Engineering\"","comment":[{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T06:37:04.211Z","text":"The point about not delegating taste or final judgement is the crucial one for me. A loop without a verifiable finish line can just keep moving confidently in the wrong direction.\n\nGiving an agent more autonomy is not the same as giving it a reliable way to know when its work is done. Tests and clear acceptance criteria can verify a lot. But architecture, maintainability and whether a solution really fits the business still require experienced judgement.\n\nWe can delegate the iteration, but not the accountability. That may be the most important rule when working with multiple agents.\n","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Markus Jessenitschnig"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":10}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T07:04:12.525Z","text":"this sounds great for well-defined tasks Addy Osmani. But what about messy real-world tasks where even the engineer isn't sure what “done” looks like? For me, the hardest part is knowing when to stop the loop when the task isn't fully deterministic.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Iqra Ramzan"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":2}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T08:59:22.030Z","text":"Clear goals + continuous feedback + verification. That’s a powerful combination.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Md Samsuzzoha"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":3}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T09:52:37.858Z","text":"I have just seen the lighthouse stats tutorial released by google developers on youtube with gemini 3.7 flash. This is really impressive specially when you can use different available mcps. Fantastic job by google. 👏","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ahsan Sarwar"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":2}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T08:40:59.246Z","text":"","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Laura McGillicuddy"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":3}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T06:48:49.609Z","text":"Well we have moved onwards to graphs already!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Harshith Nayaka L"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":3}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T07:18:58.752Z","text":"Insightful as always, thank you! ","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Gal Ziv"},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":3}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T16:27:30.276Z","text":"Hand rolled bash scripts 😂","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Brad Wolaver, Ph.D."},"interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":1}},{"@type":"Comment","datePublished":"2026-08-15T13:20:52.529Z","text":"I’m trying the loop approach with cursor using sub-agents to generate feature files with gherkin test scenarios based on product requirements, specifications and source code, but the problem is there’s over a thousand req’ts, a thousand specs, and 4 repos, and the product is quite complex, so my context is quite large. Using Opus 4.8 for covering 1/10 of the requirements cos